From 431c26b81c9e36f2ad2b30bd71d8757c5b35ba29 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 17:48:04 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Warden custom feeds: an API key in the feed address

- A custom feed address may carry $APIkey; the key is typed once in its own box, kept on the
  router in a private file (never in the list, the page source or a settings export), and put into
  the address only when the feed is fetched. A key stays with its feed when the list is reordered
  or edited, and is dropped with it.
- One new text in all 25 language packs.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
